+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Are HOA documents public record in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The recorded ones are: the declaration or master deed, the bylaws, their amendments and the rules. In Horry County the index is online and the pages are read in Conway or ordered by mail. The budget, minutes and reserve study come from the association."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I back out of buying a house because of the HOA documents?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not under a South Carolina law, which gives no right to cancel tied to the HOA papers. Your contract's review time is when to act. Virginia, Maryland and Florida law each give a buyer a set number of days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to get HOA documents?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No South Carolina law gives an association a deadline to send them. We ask the manager for the papers, the fee and the date the day you sign."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the seller have to tell me there is an HOA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, unless the sale is exempt, such as the first sale of a new home. The seller's disclosure form asks, and a yes brings the one-page HOA addendum. A missing form does not undo the contract."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does CCRs mean in an HOA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Covenants, conditions and restrictions, also written CC and Rs: the rules recorded with the declaration that come with the home. In a condo, the same rules are in the master deed."}}]}</script>
