+/* /hoa/documents/ - what to look for in HOA documents before buying in South Carolina: the red flags with their
+ * numbers, the papers to ask for and what each one tells you, what South Carolina law does and does not hand a
+ * buyer (against Virginia, Maryland, Florida and North Carolina), where Horry County keeps the recorded papers and
+ * what a copy costs, how often association rules are filed here, when the papers arrive, and what happened to
+ * Horry County owners who complained to the state.
+ *
+ * Batch 2026-11-a, Lane U. Version 1, 2026-11-04. The live page was hand-made; this spec replaces it.
+ * Facts: Blog-Brain batches/2026-11-a/hoa-documents/facts.md, verified rows only, and corrected rows only in the
+ * verifier's wording (VERIFY.md). Struck wording: hoa-documents-struck.json (no "the seller's one duty", no rules
+ * "given to a member who asks" without the carve-out, no "for a conventional loan", no 15 percent for Fannie Mae, no
+ * Maryland $250, no 716, 362 or 778, no "never received", no "the packet within 15 days").
+ * Data, never typed (website working copy, data/2026-11-a/hoa-documents/, its README.md):
+ *   chart-recorded.json    association papers filed as restrictions by year, January 2019, the last 12 months (rows 29, 30)
+ *   chart-scdca.json       Horry County complainants to SC Consumer Affairs, 2022 to 2025 (rows 31 to 33)
+ *   chart-states.json      the state comparison (rows 24 to 27); its Maryland "$250" is struck (row 25), so the
+ *                          cards below carry the verifier's wording and the file is checked, not printed
+ *   listings-counts.json   homes for sale with an association fee, counted in aggregate (row 1)
+ *   photos.json            the one photo: the Government and Justice Center, Commons, CC BY-SA 3.0 (the same files
+ *                          as /hoa/liens-and-foreclosure/, copied to this page's image folder)
+ * Kept from the live page: the title's search words, the document list (now a table with where each comes from),
+ * the SCDCA before-or-after point (now Horry County's own count), the links to reserves, special assessments,
+ * coastal insurance and condo litigation, the offer to get and read the papers, the seller-must-disclose FAQ (now
+ * with the form's 11 questions), the legal notice (shorter, no typed date).
+ * Cut: "That is an agent failure, plainly", "The fix is unglamorous", "Verified July 2026", the FAQ that repeated the body.
+ * Sibling owners: /hoa/reserves/ owns the reserve tests (one card here), /hoa/estoppel-and-transfer-fees/ owns the
+ * statement of amounts due (one step here), /hoa/liens-and-foreclosure/ shares the photo and the 31 percent line.
+ * Built by tools/mkpage.js. */
+const fs = require("fs"), path = require("path");
